        "ch1.para05",
        "ch1.para35",
        "ch1.para60"
      ],
      "text": "Invalided home from Afghanistan and short of money, Dr. Watson needs cheap lodgings. His old acquaintance Stamford introduces him to Sherlock Holmes, a brilliant, eccentric chemist who guesses Watson's past at a glance, and the two agree to share rooms."
    },
    {
      "id": "sis.recap.ch2",
      "from": "ch2.para51",
      "evidence": [
        "ch2.para01",
        "ch2.para14",
        "ch2.para24",
        "ch2.para28",
        "ch2.para50"
      ],
      "text": "Watson and Holmes settle into 221B Baker Street. Puzzled by Holmes's lopsided knowledge and many visitors, Watson finally learns that Holmes wrote an article on deduction and works as a consulting detective. Holmes then proves his point by identifying a messenger as a former Marine sergeant."
    }
  ]
